</span></td>
<td id="S4.T7.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T7.2.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T7.2.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A: There are several chemicals that can be used to treat Blast, a fungal disease that affects a variety of plants. Some commonly used chemicals for treating Blast include: Fungicides: Fungicides such as azoxystrobin, tebuconazole, and propiconazole are effective in treating Blast by controlling the growth and spread of the fungal pathogen. These fungicides can be applied as foliar sprays or drenches to provide protection to the plants.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T7.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T7.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T7.2.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T7.2.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T7.2.1.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fine-tuned LLM’s Answer</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T7.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T7.2.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T7.2.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A: The treatment of Blast disease in plants typically involves the use of fungicides. Some common chemical fungicides that are effective in treating Blast disease include: Azoxystrobin, Pyraclostrobin, Trifloxystrobin, Tebuconazole, and Propiconazole. It is important to carefully follow the instructions on the fungicide label and use personal protective equipment when applying these chemicals. Additionally, rotating between different fungicides with different modes</span>
</span></td></tr>
