</span></td>
<td id="S4.T8.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T8.2.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T8.2.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A: To treat Brownspot, you can use fungicides containing active ingredients such as azoxystrobin, propiconazole, or pyraclostrobin. Make sure to read and follow the manufacturer’s instructions and safety precautions when using these chemicals. Additionally, good cultural practices such as proper irrigation and avoiding over-fertilization can help prevent the spread of Brownspot.</span>
