<span id="S4.T8.2.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T8.2.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A: There are several chemicals that can be used to effectively treat Brownspot, a fungal disease that commonly affects plants. Some options include: Chlorothalonil: This chemical is a broad-spectrum fungicide that can help control Brownspot and other fungal diseases on plants; Propiconazole: Another effective fungicide that can be used to treat Brownspot and other fungal diseases; Copper-based fungicides: These can also be effective in controlling Brownspot, especially when used preventatively.</span>
</span></td></tr>
