</span></td>
<td id="S4.T9.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T9.2.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T9.2.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A: To treat bacterial leaf blight in plants, you can use chemicals such as copper-based fungicides, antibiotics like streptomycin, and bactericides like oxytetracycline. It is important to follow the instructions on the product label and apply the chemicals at the recommended rate and frequency to effectively control the disease. Additionally, rotating between different chemical treatments can help prevent the development of resistance in the bacteria.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T9.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
